{"name":"After the Storm","hex":"#33616a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"after","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Behind; later in time; following."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Subsequently to; following in time; later than.","Subsequently to and as a result of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after"},{"term":"storm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any disturbed state of the atmosphere causing destructive or unpleasant weather, especially one affecting the earth's surface involving strong winds (leading to high waves at sea) and usually lightning, thunder, and precipitation.","A heavy fall of precipitation (hail, rain, or snow) or bout of lightning and thunder without strong winds; a hail storm, rainstorm, snowstorm, or thunderstorm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Preceded by the dummy subject it: to have strong winds and usually lightning and thunder, and/or hail, rain, or snow.","To make (someone or something) stormy; to agitate (someone or something) violently.\n\n\nTo disturb or trouble (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm"}],"entries":[{"title":"After the Storm (1915 film)","blocks":[{"text":"After the Storm is a 1915 American silent short drama film directed by B. Reeves Eason."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/After_the_Storm_%281915%29.png/330px-After_the_Storm_%281915%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_the_Storm_(1915_film)","wikidata":"Q4690688"},{"title":"After the Storm (1928 film)","blocks":[{"text":"After the Storm is a 1928 American silent drama film directed by George B. Seitz. A print of the film exists at the Cinematheque Royale de Belgique."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/After_the_Storm_still_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-After_the_Storm_still_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_the_Storm_(1928_film)","wikidata":"Q4690685"},{"title":"After the Storm (Monica album)","blocks":[{"text":"After the Storm is the fourth album by the American singer Monica. It was first released on June 17, 2003, through J Records. Developed over three years amid personal struggles, the project faced multiple delays following the moderate success and bootlegging of the album's previous incarnation All Eyez on Me (2002), leading Monica to scrap much of the original material and start anew with collaborators, including Jazze Pha, BAM & Ryan, and Missy Elliott, the latter of whom served as executive producer and re-shaped much of After the Storm with her sample-heavy signature production and creative vision."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/After_the_Storm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_the_Storm_(Monica_album)","wikidata":"Q514247"},{"title":"Storm","blocks":[{"text":"A storm is any disturbed state of the natural environment or the atmosphere of an astronomical body. It may be marked by significant disruptions to normal conditions such as strong wind, tornadoes, hail, thunder and lightning, heavy precipitation, heavy freezing rain, strong winds, wind transporting some substance through the atmosphere such as in a dust storm, among other forms of severe weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg/330px-Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm","wikidata":"Q81054"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Missy_Elliott_2006.jpg/500px-Missy_Elliott_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":